  "issue_number": 5,
  "issue_title": "fix: apply SVF scales in submission pack and cached pr_eval",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n\nFixes a critical correctness bug where **70% of the composite PR score** (cached hidden eval) was computed without the miner'\\''s trained SVF scales.\n\n## Root cause\n\n1. **`pack_submission.py`** called `policy.svf.current_scales()`, which does not exist on `SVFAdapter`. The `AttributeError` handler silently wrote all-ones SVF scales to every submission, discarding half of the optimized \u03b8 vector.\n2. **`pr_eval.py` cached eval** encoded questions with the raw encoder (identity SVF) and only loaded head weights, so routing decisions did not match training-time `policy.configure(\u03b8)`.\n\nTraining optimizes both the head (6,144 params) and SVF scales (7,168 params). Submissions and cached eval were effectively evaluating head-only routing on the wrong hidden states.\n\n## Fix approach\n\n- **`pack_submission.py`**: Extract `(head_W, svf_scales)` directly from `best_theta.npy` via `params.unpack()` \u2014 no GPU required, no silent fallback.\n- **`pr_eval.py`**: Configure the full policy (head + SVF) before cached/audit eval and route via `policy.decide()` so hidden states match training.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Submissions now ship the actual trained SVF scales.\n- Cached and audit accuracy reflect the full coordinator as miners trained it.\n- Composite scoring (70% hidden + 15% live) becomes consistent with the CMA-ES objective.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdded `tests/test_svf_submission.py` covering \u03b8 unpack, pack extraction, and cached-eval routing via policy.\n\nLocal validation: **84 tests passed** (`pytest tests/`).\n\n## Risks / tradeoffs\n\n- Previously packed submissions with identity SVF will score differently after re-pack. Miners should re-run `pack_submission.py` from their `best_theta.npy`.\n- Novelty gate still compares head routing on raw encoder hidden states (5% weight); unchanged in this PR to keep scope minimal.",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-11T04:16:00.000Z",
  "test_cmd": [
    "python",
    "-m",
    "pytest",
    "--tb=short",
    "-q",
    "tests/test_pr_eval_cached_transcript.py"
  ],
